pared to introducing new business processes, attempts to copy existing processes are</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t3-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>more attractive.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t3-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>more frequent.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t3-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>more straightforward.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span>Most research into the repetition of success in business has</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t3-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>been done outside the United States.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t3-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>produced consistent findings.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t3-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>related to only a few contexts.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span>What does the speaker say about consulting experts?</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c8-t3-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>Too few managers ever do it.</span></div><div class=\"sourc